<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Parliament of Southern Ireland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1921–1922</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Parliament of Southern Ireland was the home-rule legislature created for the 26 counties of Southern Ireland by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/government-of-ireland-act-1920">Government of Ireland Act 1920</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sinn-fein">Sinn Féin</a> won 124 of the 128 seats in its House of Commons unopposed in May 1921 but sat instead as the Second <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dail-eireann">Dáil</a>, so only the four members for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a> University and the appointed senators attended. It met only twice before giving way to the Irish Free State.</p></div>
